  "revised": "2026-11-10",
  "source": "KRON, \"Protocolo Modbus – Ikron 03-D\", rev. 1.0 (May 2018)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Protocolo Modbus – Ikron 03-D",
      "version": "1.0",
      "date": "2018-05",
      "url": "https://es.kron.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/Protocolo-Modbus-Ikron-03-D-1.1.pdf",
      "note": "linked in issue #140"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Read with FC03 and write with FC06 or FC16. The document numbers the registers from 40001 and gives the hex address as the number minus 40001 (40015 is 0x000E), which is what this map uses.",
    "Values are IEEE 754 floats sent with the most significant byte first (the document's example reads 43 66 4C CD as 230.3 V).",
    "The factory settings are 9600 bps, 8 data bits, even parity and 1 stop bit (8E1). The document does not give a default slave address: 1 is its example.",
    "The document does not state units for power or energy, so those registers have none. The date and time registers (0x003C to 0x003F, BCD) and the firmware and hardware versions (floats at 0x0004 and 0x0006) are not mapped: the table in the document is garbled there."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "E",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
